@startuml
title Client-Server Model: One Established TCP Connection
participant "Client process" as C
participant "Server process" as S
S -> S: socket() -> bind() -> listen()
C -> C: socket()
C -> S: connect(): initiate connection establishment
S -> S: accept(): obtain a connected socket\nfrom the listening socket's queue
C <-> S: byte stream via read()/write()\napplications define message boundaries
C -> C: close(): release this descriptor
C -> S: TCP termination when applicable\n(not the close() system call itself)
S -> S: read() may return 0 after peer EOF;\nclose connected socket when finished
note over S
Listening socket remains separate and can accept other connections.
Errors, partial I/O, buffering and half-close are omitted here.
end note
@enduml
